Now I have a good understanding of the bug. Let me trace through the flow:

1. User creates a Trip and saves it
2. User edits the Trip, modifying the date
3. User presses Save

Looking at `ManageTripFragment.verifyUserInput()`:
```java
@Override
public boolean verifyUserInput() {
    // make sure the new trip doesn't overlap any existing trips
    if ((mDateChanged || !isEditing()) && Logbook.tripExists(getNewTrip())) {
        AlertUtils.showError(getActivity(), R.string.error_trip_date);
        return false;
    }
    ...
}
```

And `tripExists(Trip trip)`:
```java
public static boolean tripExists(Trip trip) {
    ArrayList<UserDefineObject> trips = getTrips();

    for (UserDefineObject object : trips)
        if (trip.overlapsTrip((Trip)object))
            return true;

    return false;
}
```

The `overlapsTrip` method:
```java
public boolean overlapsTrip(Trip trip) {
    return trip.getStartDate().before(mEndDate) && trip.getEndDate().after(mStartDate);
}
```

I see the issue now. When editing a trip, the `tripExists` check compares the modified trip against all existing trips in the database, including the trip being edited itself. Since the dates have changed, the overlap detection might incorrectly flag the trip as conflicting with itself or with other trips that don't actually overlap. the same dates, it should still pass the overlap check since the trip shouldn't be considered conflicting with itself during validation. The `tripExists` method needs to exclude the trip currently being edited from its check, otherwise it will always find an overlap and return true, blocking any date edits. Looking at the overlap logic in `ManageTripFragment.verifyUserInput()`, there's a condition checking `mDateChanged || !isEditing()`, which means the overlap validation only runs when dates have actually changed or when adding a new trip, not when editing without date modifications.

However, the `tripExists` method itself doesn't account for the trip being edited—it checks all trips in the database, including the one being modified, so it will always detect an overlap with itself since a trip always overlaps with itself based on the date comparison logic.

The fix is to pass the editing ID to `tripExists` so it can skip that specific trip during the overlap check. Since `editTrip()` uses the ID to identify which record to update, the method needs to know which trip to exclude from its validation. This way, when editing a trip without changing dates, or when modifying dates to something that doesn't conflict with other trips, the validation will work correctly.

Now I need to examine the `QueryHelper.updateUserDefine` method to see if there are any other potential issues with how the update is being performed.

